<title>USA: Iraq nears $2.14 bln U.N. oil sales limit.</title>
<headline>Iraq nears $2.14 bln U.N. oil sales limit.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-04-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Iraqi oil sales are within $130 million of the $2.142 billion target set for the oil-for-food accord, which runs for six months to June 7, according to U.N. officials Wednesday.</p>
<p>The 44th contract, a 350,000 barrel spot contract for Chevron Corp to lift Basrah Light from Mina al-Bakr in the Middle East Gulf to the U.S., brings the total volume of approved oil contracts to just over 116 million barrels.</p>
<p>The U.N. also is expected to approve today May contract prices for Iraq, which will follow the increased discounts recently announced for Saudi Arab Light crude, diplomats said.</p>
</text>
